## Key Results

### ERL identifies financial risk beyond return probability

![Loss Capture Curve](images/ERL_loss_capture_curve.png)

ERL-based ranking captured 16.6% of total financial exposure
within the top 10% of transactions, compared with 12.5% using
return probability alone.

### What drives return losses?

![ERL Reason Breakdown](images/ERL_reason_breakdown.png)

The reason-level analysis shows that financial exposure varies
substantially across product categories, with defect-related costs
being the dominant driver for many product types.

## Validation & Limitations

![ML Validation](images/ERL_ml_validation.png)

Neither probability nor ERL was a strong predictor of whether an
individual transaction would actually be returned. This reinforces
an important distinction: ERL was designed to prioritise expected
financial exposure rather than replace a return-probability model.
